Z||000000||85ZainoGT||10-30-2001||12:26 PM||||Does anyone know who makes power pulleys for us?  thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-30-2001||12:52 PM||||Check out the fiero store... they've got one!  <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com</A>   <P>$80 for the kit: <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo_pegasus.asp?number=52304&variation=&aitem=19&mitem=23" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo_pegasus.asp?number=52304&variation=&aitem=19&mitem=23</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||85ZainoGT||10-30-2001||09:29 PM||||awesome thanks, for he people who have them...  are they worth it?  are there any other places to get them?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-30-2001||09:43 PM||||I had one but ditched it when I started working of the supercharger project- I needed a large pulley to drive the blower and that pulley would not fit alongside the power pulley. The only thing I noticed was my car's alternator charges full at idle now and runs slightly cooler with the factory pulley back on it. Oh, and with the power pulley and stock intake I pulled off a G-tech quarter mile in 14.71- when I put the stocker back on I can only manage a 14.77||||reg||1
Z||000004||Patrick's Dad||10-30-2001||10:11 PM||||I have one on the project. I don't have access to a dyno, so I don't know if it was one of those "afterglow" type of mods. The mostly stock 2.8 seemed to react a little quicker, but there was no kick in the pants type of thing. It didn't hurt the alternator or the water pump for me. Can't say anything about the compressor, that had been gone for a while.<P>I'll likely move it to the 3.4.||||reg||1
Z||000005||recluse||10-30-2001||11:12 PM||||Ive got one.  I cant say that I feel any power increase but just the fact that its smaller and alot lighter tells me that it must be freeing up at least a little power.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spiff||10-31-2001||12:27 AM||||The company's name that makes the underdrive pulleys is Auto Specialties Performance . They are the same as the Fiero Store pulleys but you get a Alternator pulley also. Plus they are cheaper.<BR>Here is the summit part # and price ASP-845202 PULLEY SET 69.39. I think you will have to call to do a special order.<BR>Also here is a link to ASP and there e-mail address   <A HREF="http://www.aspracing.com/intro.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aspracing.com/intro.htm</A>       asp@aspracing.com <BR> <BR>It is a 24% crank and 23% alternator so it slows the alternator almost 50% and the water pump only 24%.. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||TRiAD||10-31-2001||12:32 AM||||<I>Fiero Year Engine Pulley Description Full Charge Hard<BR>Blk Alum <BR>85-88 2.8 25% Crank (full charge 900 RPM) ASP845200<BR>$59.95 <BR>85-88 2.8 25% Crank<BR>23% Alternator (full charge 1100 RPM) ASP845202<BR>$79.95</I><P>877-928-8678. <P>Sounds good, but how did you get the lower price?<BR>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">    <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Klown||10-31-2001||04:48 AM||||Hey Triad.  What's the difference between the two sets?  Is one better than the other?||||reg||5
Z||000009||montage||10-31-2001||08:14 AM||||I have one and IMHO it is well worth it. I did notice a big difference in shifting from 2-3, before the pulley it would drop out of the power band, now it stays right up there. After I put the pulley on I purchased a G-tech and my best 0-60 time is 7.19 secs with an 88 formula 5-speed 98,000 mi no other mods.||||reg||1
Z||000010||TRiAD||10-31-2001||08:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Klown:<BR><B>Hey Triad.  What's the difference between the two sets?  Is one better than the other?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 2 sets I listed are 1) without the alternator pulley and 2) with it. <P>The "with the alternator pulley" kit is the same one he listed above. <P>||||reg||1
